      "strengthsSections": [
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Supports durability by reducing damage taken",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/181131_mh4w8.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "This is also a valuable effect, but Elisa can reduce damage taken by a single ally, greatly contributing to the party's durability.",
            "It is often combined with recovery, so by giving it to a defender, it will recover the wall role, reduce damage taken, and have a strong support effect, so basically you should use it in combination with the defender.",
            "The Effect RES you receive as a bonus will also make you stronger against debuffs, so it's definitely a nice effect."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Additional turns make it easier to reuse skills",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/181654_koyh0.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Elisa can generate an additional turn by accumulating the upheaval stack to the maximum, making it relatively easy to reuse each skill.",
            "Also, since you can apply multiple turbulent stacks with skills, it is also a powerful point that you can create a smooth flow of skill use → additional turn → skill reuse."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Powerful with gauntlet",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/181932_qzy7v.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Elisa's main battlefield is the gauntlet, which is especially powerful in defense battles in strategy battles. Elisa does not have any firepower buffs, but she is particularly good at durability, so she can stabilize the party's durability.",
            "Firepower is not necessary in a defensive battle, and it is recommended to form a party that will not be defeated, so Elisa is one of the most powerful supporters.",
            "It's relatively easy to choose carefully, so if you have it, it's a good idea to actively utilize it."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "There is no total recovery",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/181732_cem4v.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Please note that while it specializes in single-target recovery, it does not have overall recovery, so it can be a little difficult to use.",
            "If it's a gauntlet, you can deal with it by forming two supporters, but it's not suitable for bosses who use a lot of all-out attacks, so be sure to use a supporter that can cover the whole area, such as Dress Asherah."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Appearance in PvE content is limited.",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "While being able to revive allies is a strength, it also means that the enemy is strong enough to cause an ally to be defeated, and even if you fight the enemy in that state, you will most likely be defeated.",
            "Also, in PvE, the basics are to have a quick attack with an attacker-heavy formation, or to form a supporter that emphasizes firepower such as Dress Asherah or Emily, so keep in mind that Elisa, who has no firepower-related effects, will have limited opportunities to play an active role."
          ]
        }
      ],
