      "strengthsSections": [
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Special Skill 3 consecutive hits are powerful",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/115747_1e54v.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Omega has a unique buff called \"Power Up Star\", and depending on the number of stacks of this buff, it is powerful because it can fire up to three consecutive Special Skills.",
            "Since it attacks all over, it is difficult to make the most of it against a single opponent, but it is extremely strong against multiple battles and against opponents that require an all-out attack such as \"Carbonpunk Can\", so it is important to consider the location and use it."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h4",
          "title": "Toughness cannot be removed",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Omega's Special Skill does not have Toughness Damage, so it is not possible to reduce Toughness all at once using repeated attacks.",
            "However, of course, you can reduce Toughness when you have an attribute advantage, so you will be able to have a more advantageous battle against Moon Attribute."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Overall skill CT is light.",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/115638_c8gj7.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Omega's Special Skill and Ultimate Skill both have a light CT3 of 3, and although there are no additional turns, it is easy to reuse skills.",
            "It's nice that it's easy to maintain the attack buff, and the speed buff from the power-up star is also excellent, so the fact that it's relatively easy to fight around can be said to be its strength."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Formation restrictions are heavy",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/115921_kx5d8.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "If you want to make the most of power-up stars, you need to strengthen your allies other than Omega with Star Attributes, so the formation restrictions can be said to be heavy.",
            "The only way to accumulate jumping stacks is to use Ultimate Skill and Basic Skill other than the attacks of Star Attribute allies, and it takes too much time to show your true potential, so it is recommended to have at least 1 or 2 Star Attributes."
          ]
        }
      ],
