      "strengthsSections": [
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Delay enemy actions with skill seal",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Bellreath's Ultimate Skill can seal the enemy's skills with CT (Special Skill, Ultimate Skill) for 2 turns, so it is also possible to delay the enemy's actions.",
            "It is a powerful effect, especially when the enemy's skills are troublesome, such as in PvP, so it can also be used as a debuffer in conjunction with the removal of reinforcement described below."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h4",
          "title": "Firepower increases depending on jumping stack",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "When the jump stack is at maximum, the Ultimate Skill's Damage Dealt increases by 30%, so you can expect not only interference but also pure firepower.",
            "Three jumping stacks can be given with Special Skills, but the rest must be accumulated with Basic Skills, so the drawback is that it takes a little time to take advantage of the effect.",
            "Including the aforementioned passive effect, it can be used as a powerful effect in multiple waves where battles naturally tend to drag on."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Excellent at removing enemy reinforcements",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "This is also an effect of the Ultimate Skill, but it can remove the strengthened state of the enemy.",
            "Basically, you will need to target the enemy you want to apply the skill seal to, so be careful not to make a mistake when selecting the target for the skill."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h4",
          "title": "Powerful as a meta for nasty effects",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/114424_0gr5o.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "At the Bell lease event, an effect called \"immortality\" that allows you to survive with HP +1 was confirmed.",
            "Basically, you have to endure until the effect wears off, but this effect can be canceled by removing the reinforcement.",
            "Considering that such troublesome effects will continue to increase in the future, there is a possibility that reinforcement removal will become a very powerful meta skill."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h4",
          "title": "Reinforcement is canceled after damage",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Please note that the decision to remove the reinforcement is made after the damage has been done, so it is not possible to punch through immortality or immunity.",
            "Since it requires an attack from another ally after it is released, that point can be said to be a little disappointing."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "There is also a line of pushing hard due to the drop in accuracy.",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "This is intended for everyday use, not PvP, but the Special Skill and Basic Skill Nova Burst can reduce the enemy's accuracy.",
            "The effect value is also not bad at 30%, so depending on your luck, you may be able to greatly reduce the damage taken by applying it to the boss.",
            "If you have a situation where you are stuck in a strategy, you may want to consider using Bell Lease."
          ]
        }
      ],
