      "strengthsSections": [
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Applies electric shock when attacking allies",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/135159_vu0q5.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Gwen has the ability to apply a unique stack called \"Electric Shock\" to herself when attacking an ally, and activates her Special Skill when her unique stack reaches its maximum.",
            "Although the electric shock itself has no special effect, it accumulates just by attacking allies, so depending on the party, it is possible to use special skills frequently."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h4",
          "title": "Compatible with characters that require a lot of work(Great)",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Since this is when an ally attacks, you should be able to accumulate stacks more quickly if you team up with a character who takes a lot of steps.",
            "There are quite a few characters that require a lot of work, such as Professor M who will be implemented in the same event and Swimsuit Smile who has the same attribute, so I would like to pair her with a character that can take advantage of Gwen's skill effects."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h4",
          "title": "Single firepower is modest",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "On the other hand, Special Skill has a modest multiplier of 70%, so the amount of damage per attack is modest.",
            "Gwen alone or in combination with a character who doesn't have many moves can be a little heavy, so be careful when organizing your party."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Waiting at the scene, treated as hidden",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/135516_x5ajy.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "When Gwen starts a battle and uses her Ultimate Skill, she will be given a buff called ``stand by on scene,'' but this buff is treated as a stealth buff, allowing her to be out of the enemy's attack target.",
            "Also, unlike stealth, it is extremely powerful in that it cannot be canceled even if attacked, and on top of that, it is possible to receive hidden-related buffs without any problems.",
            "Preemptive defense cannot be ignored, but it is basically limited to PvP, so in PvE, this on-site standby is a more convenient buff to use."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h4",
          "title": "Always placed in the vanguard",
          "imageUrl": "",
          "paragraphs": [
            "When taking advantage of this stealth ability and teaming up with Fei and others, be sure to place Gwei in the vanguard. By placing it in the vanguard, the vanguard effectively targets only one character, making that character more likely to be targeted.",
            "If you place it in the rear, it will be difficult to take advantage of the hidden effect, so be careful."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Unconditional special trigger with Ultimate Skill",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/135828_6ze5n.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "His Ultimate Skill has an unconditional Special Skill trigger, and he can expect high firepower with that move.",
            "It already takes a lot of moves thanks to the Passive effect, but it is also great that you can increase the number of moves even more thanks to this skill.",
            "Considering that the Ultimate Skill's multiplier is 115%, which is an average multiplier, and that the Special Skill is superimposed on it, the Ultimate Skill's firepower can be said to be quite high."
          ]
        },
        {
          "level": "h3",
          "title": "Firepower increases or decreases depending on the party",
          "imageUrl": "https://appmedia.jp/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/141627_d2156.webp",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Please note that Gwen's firepower will increase or decrease depending on the party, as Special Skills are activated depending on the number of attacks made by allies.",
            "If you team up with a character that requires fewer moves, Gwen's number of attacks will decrease accordingly, so be sure to create a party that requires more moves."
          ]
        }
      ],
